{
  "requirement": "Habeas's bundled agent instructions MUST direct agents to run Cargo doctests\nseparately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `requirements.test-coverage.guidance.doctests` has one MUST. Habeas's bundled agent instructions must direct agents to run Cargo doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`. The instructions are the bundled skills and the agent SOP. The requirement's `:impl:` anchor names `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_default_to_process_coverage_and_keep_artifacts_disposable]` carries `{test}` for this requirement. Its assertions match the obligation:\n- For each of the `habeas`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` skills, it asserts that the collapsed skill text contains `` `cargo test --doc --workspace` ``. The text comes from `bundled_skill`, which joins `SKILL.md` and the reference files. Whitespace collapsing means line wrapping cannot hide a miss.\n- For the `habeas` skill, it asserts the full directive: \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\". This checks the \"separately\" part, not only the command string.\n- For `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, it asserts \"run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n- For `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`, which it reads with `include_str!`, it asserts \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n\n**Other instruction files.** I searched `habeas-refactor`, `habeas-requirements` and the other SOPs for doctest, `cargo test` and `nextest` guidance. `habeas-refactor` and `habeas-requirements` have none, and the other two SOPs have none either. Since those files give no test-running guidance at all, no doctest direction is owed there. Only `approved-implementation.sop.md` gives such guidance, and it is covered.\n\n**Assessment.** A regression that dropped or reworded the doctest directive in any file that carries it would fail one of these assertions. The test has no `{test}` marking gap, since the marker sits on the test function itself. The text has no ambiguity or exemption that needs separate handling, and nothing is delegated to another requirement. I found no adequacy gap.",
